        "content": "**Description:** Mirafold is a browser-based UI wrapper for terminal coding agents including Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini CLI. It transforms \"dense scrollback into a clear, readable interface\" while preserving the underlying agent's functionality. The tool renders \"live cards, charts, and dashboards you can pin and watch update\" rather than traditional terminal text output.\n\n**Launch Status/Date:** The software is currently available. The site references a \"7-day free trial\" for the Pro tier, and video content is dated July 30, 2026. It's distributed as open source software under the MIT license.\n\n**Key Details:**\n\n- **Installation:** Via npm (`npm i -g mirafold`), requires Node.js 22+\n- **Pricing:** Free tier (open source, local-only) or Pro tier ($12 monthly or $99 yearly) for remote access via encrypted relay\n- **Architecture:** Local daemon processes agent commands; API keys remain in local environment variables\n- **Security:** Uses sandboxed iframes with restricted CSP for arbitrary UI generation; agent output renders only into designated output zones\n- **Multi-session:** Supports running multiple concurrent agent sessions with centralized \"mission control\" grid view\n- **Cross-platform:** Works on macOS, Linux, and Windows\n- **Privacy:** API keys never reach browser; Pro relay sees only ciphertext and connection metadata"
