        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# wallfacer - Terminal Session Manager\n\n## Description & Launch\nwallfacer is a terminal session manager for multiple AI coding tools, including Claude Code, Cursor CLI, Kiro CLI, and Codex. It was created on July 28, 2026.\n\n## What It Does for Claude Code Users\nClaude Code stores conversations as \"untitled JSONL file[s] under ~/.claude/projects/\" making them difficult to organize and find. wallfacer solves this by indexing all sessions and providing a management interface.\n\n**Key capabilities:**\n- View every session in one place, sorted by recency\n- Rename sessions, tag them, and group them into projects\n- Search across titles, first prompts, directories, projects, and tags\n- Resume previous sessions by ID prefix or title\n- Delete sessions safely (moves to trash; only `--purge` is permanent)\n\n## Technical Details\n- Written in Go (requires Go 1.22+)\n- Stores metadata in SQLite at `~/.local/share/wallfacer/`\n- Works read-only, never touching agent files directly\n- Offers both a full-screen TUI and CLI subcommands\n- Released under MIT license\n\n## Installation\nAvailable via Homebrew (`brew install pradipta/wallfacer/wallfacer`) or Go (`go install github.com/pradipta/wallfacer@latest`)."
      }
    ]
